{
  "title": "img vs. figure",
  "content": "The `<img>` tag in HTML is used to embed a simple image directly into a webpage. It requires a `src` attribute to specify the image source. On the other hand, the `<figure>` element represents self-contained content, like an image, illustration, diagram, code snippet, etc., that is referenced as a single unit. It is typically used with the `<figcaption>` element to provide a caption for the figure.\r\n\r\nVisit the following resources to learn more:\r\n\r\n- [@article@The Ultimate Guide to Using HTML Figure Elements](https://www.dhiwise.com/post/the-ultimate-guide-to-using-html-figure-elements)\r\n- [@video@When to use image, figure and picture tag in html](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xn5_gDQFyJg)"
}